   "stem": {
      "text": "Let h(x) = sqrt(x + 3) / (x^2 - 4x). Consider the largest interval that contains x = 1 and on which h is continuous. How many integers does that interval contain?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 3
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The radicand requires x >= -3, and the denominator x^2 - 4x = x(x - 4) is zero at x = 0 and x = 4, so the excluded inputs are x < -3, x = 0 and x = 4.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            "x",
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               4
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "h is a quotient of a square root function and a polynomial, each continuous on its domain, so h is continuous at every input of its domain [-3, 0) U (0, 4) U (4, infinity).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            "x",
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The piece of the domain that contains x = 1 is the open interval (0, 4), and both endpoints are open because h is undefined there.",
         "mathjson": 4
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The integers in (0, 4) are 1, 2 and 3.",
         "mathjson": 3
      }
   ],
